to":"Clapham Junction Rail Station","towards":"Watford Junction Rail Station"},{"mode":"national-rail","line":"South Western Railway","minutes":8,"summary":"South Western Railway","from":"Clapham Junction Rail Station","to":"London Waterloo Rail Station","towards":"London Waterloo Rail Station"},{"mode":"walking","line":null,"minutes":4,"summary":"Walk","from":"London Waterloo Rail Station","to":"12A MEPHAM STREET, LONDON","towards":null}],"reason":null,"name":"London Waterloo"}],"bestHub":{"name":"London Waterloo","minutes":49},"missing":[]},"summary":"Oaks Estate Agents are delighted to present this beautifully presented, furnished two-bedroom garden flat on Melrose Avenue in Norbury. Set within an attractive period property, this inviting home offers approximately 748 sq ft of accommodation, with the added benefits of a separate study, a generous private garden and an off-street parking space on the driveway.<br /><br />\rThe property combines character with a contemporary finish, creating a home with plenty of personality and a practical layout. At the front, the bright open-plan kitchen and reception room features a large bay window with fitted shutters, allowing natural light to fill the space. Soft green walls, wood-effect flooring and a decorative ceiling rose give the room a welcoming feel, with space to relax, entertain and enjoy everyday life.<br /><br />The kitchen is neatly arranged along one side of the reception room, with white cabinetry, contrasting worktops, a tiled splashback and a built-in oven and hob. Its open-plan position makes it a sociable space, keeping the cooking and living areas connected.<br /><br />There are two bedrooms, including a generously proportioned principal bedroom measuring approximately 14ft 2in by 10ft 10in. A separate study at the rear provides a useful additional room, particularly for anyone working from home or wanting some separation between their working day and living space. The accommodation also includes a modern shower room with a glass shower enclosure, contemporary tiling and vanity storage, alongside a separate utility area with access outside.<br /><br />The private rear garden is a real highlight. Extending approximately 49ft, it offers a substantial lawn and space for outdoor seating, summer entertaining or simply enjoying a quiet moment outside. Having this much outdoor space alongside a furnished flat is a particularly appealing combination, while the driveway parking space adds another practical benefit.<br /><br />Melrose Avenue is well placed for enjoying everything Norbury has to offer. London Road provides a varied selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés and restaurants, making everyday essentials and an evening out easy to fit around a busy schedule. The area’s mix of independent businesses and places to eat gives it a lively neighbourhood feel, while Streatham’s wider choice of shopping, dining and leisure facilities offers further options nearby.<br /><br />For commuters, Norbury station provides rail connections to London Victoria and London Bridge, making the location convenient for travelling into central London. Local bus routes also connect the surrounding neighbourhoods, providing options for journeys towards Streatham and Croydon.<br /><br />Outdoor space is another attraction of the area, with Norbury Park and Norbury Hall Park offering opportunities for walks and time outdoors beyond your own garden. Together with the local amenities and transport connections, this makes Norbury an appealing location for tenants looking for a balance of convenience and space.<br /><br />With two bedrooms, a dedicated study, private garden and driveway parking, this furnished Norbury flat offers considerably more than just its living accommodation. Contact Oaks Estate Agents to arrange your viewing.<br /><br />","keyFeatures":["Two-bedroom ground floor maisonette","Furnished","Off-street parking space on the driveway","Private rear garden extending approximately 49f